    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "text": "When s=1 and d=3, the model learns maps covering the full spectral region within the Karpelevič region of B_3\\B_2 up to error ε(s=1), and also covers real eigenvalues on interval [-1,1] (Karpelevič region of B_2).",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000071"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "text": "When s=2, the model covers a larger region with a smaller spectral gap, i.e., ε(s=2) < ε(s=1).",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000071"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "text": "Bounding the spectrum stabilizes gradients, as discussed in Appendix B.8 and prior work.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000072"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "text": "We evaluate expressivity by using the spectrum of matrices constructed with P_M as a surrogate, measuring how many unique matrices can be spanned by their eigenvalues.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000072"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "text": "Exact volume of B_d is unknown, so we rely on surrogate measures for expressivity of doubly stochastic matrices.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000072"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": null,
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source"
    },
    {
      "kind": "claim",
      "text": "Spectral reach of H^{res} matrices constructed using method M is defined as the set {λ∈ℂ | H^{res} v = λ v, H^{res}=P_M(...), v≠0}.",
